    <comment>New package python-torchvision for openSUSE:Factory from science:machinelearning (ComfyUI cone). pluskalm is the science:machinelearning package maintainer.

New to Factory (devel science:machinelearning was 0.18.1; this is 0.27.0 matching Factory python-torch 2.12.0).

INTERDEPENDENT REQUESTS - please stage together (ComfyUI cone):
  * sr#1372737 python-av (need &gt;= 16 for comfyui)
  * sr#1372780 python-trampoline
  * sr#1372789 python-kornia-rs
  * sr#1372790 python-comfyui-frontend-package
  * sr#1372791 python-comfyui-workflow-templates-core
  * sr#1372793 python-comfyui-workflow-templates-json
  * sr#1372794 python-comfyui-workflow-templates-media-api
  * sr#1372795 python-comfyui-workflow-templates-media-assets-01
  * sr#1372796 python-comfyui-workflow-templates-media-image
  * sr#1372797 python-comfyui-workflow-templates-media-other
  * sr#1372798 python-comfyui-workflow-templates-media-video
  * sr#1372799 python-comfy-aimdo
  * sr#1372800 comfyui
  * sr#1372804 python-comfyui-workflow-templates
  * sr#1372805 python-torchaudio
  * this batch: python-comfyui-embedded-docs, python-comfy-kitchen,
    python-torchsde, python-kornia, python-torchvision, python-spandrel

Fri Aug 21 08:56:25 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal &lt;mpluskal@suse.com&gt;

- Update to 0.27.0 (matches Factory python-torch 2.12.0):
  * Add lanczos interpolation for v2.Resize on CPU (AVX2/NEON)
  * Add KeyPoints and rotated bounding-box support in v2
    transforms
  * Add GIF and WEBP image decoders; decode_image() accepts paths
  * Resize can target the longest edge via max_size
  * Remove the video_reader backend (use TorchCodec / pyav)
  * Vectorize masks_to_boxes; add rotated-box IoU
  * Fix v2.ElasticTransform normalization and bbox clamping
- Add fix-gif-decoder-oob.patch (pytorch/vision#9520, from 0.28):
  * GIF decoder heap OOB read/write on crafted images
    (GHSA-vp9x-48wq-4wc3; no CVE assigned)
- Build CPU-only against Factory torch (FORCE_CUDA=0, no NVJPEG)
- Drop ffmpeg BuildRequires: video_reader was removed upstream
- Switch the build to %pyproject_wheel / %pyproject_install
- Run %check outside the source tree so the compiled _C extension
  is imported
- Declare runtime Requires for numpy, Pillow and torch (the
  generator does not pick them up from this setuptools wheel)
- Strip unused shebangs from imported .py modules

Fri Aug 21 08:47:56 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal &lt;mpluskal@suse.com&gt;

- Build against distro ffmpeg via pkgconfig(libavcodec) and friends instead of the retired ffmpeg-6 packages.
</comment>
